# Kubernetes Top 50 Interview Questions

# Kubernetes Basics
1. What is Kubernetes and why do we need it?
Kubernetes (K8s) is an open-source container orchestration platform used to deploy, manage, scale, and monitor containerized applications automatically.
It was originally developed by Google and is now maintained by the Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF).
> Why do we need Kubernetes?
Automates application deployment.
Automatically scales applications based on traffic.
Restarts failed containers (self-healing).
Distributes traffic using load balancing.
Performs rolling updates and rollbacks with minimal downtime.

2. Explain Kubernetes Architecture.
Kubernetes follows a Master-Worker architecture.
It has two main components:
> 1. Control Plane (Master Node)
The Control Plane manages the entire Kubernetes cluster.
Components:
API Server – Entry point for all Kubernetes commands.
etcd – Stores cluster configuration and state.
Scheduler – Decides which worker node will run a Pod.
Controller Manager – Monitors the cluster and maintains the desired state.
Cloud Controller Manager:	Integrates Kubernetes with cloud services

> 2. Worker Node
Worker nodes run the application containers.
Components:
Pods – Run the application containers.
Kubelet – Communicates with the Control Plane and manages Pods.
Container Runtime – Runs containers (such as containerd or CRI-O).
Kube Proxy – Handles networking and load balancing between Pods.

